ok    grade    estate-showcase grades the fixture catalogue (0 GAP rows) and --check refuses a stale page  (10s)
ok    ha       14/14 graded surface(s) survive losing one node (6 waived)  (6s)
      WAIVED    availability otto.${ESTATE_ZONE}        hermes-agent/hermes-agent-gateway: One Telegram token may be long-polled by exactly one process (two are 409s on both, gateway.yaml:18-23) and HERMES_HOME is a ReadWriteOnce volume holding state.db, so replicas 2 here is an outage, not a fix. The remedy is a webhook or a lease, not a number. (chidionyema/idp#547)
      WAIVED    availability signoz.${ESTATE_ZONE}      observability/signoz: SigNoz stands on one ClickHouse; two replicas against a single database moves the single point of failure rather than removing it. HA here is a ClickHouse topology change, not a replica count. (chidionyema/idp#544)
      WAIVED    availability hc.${ESTATE_ZONE}          flux-system/webhook-receiver: The service behind this route is Flux's own notification-controller, rendered by clusters/oke/flux-system/gotk-components.yaml -- a path this gate does not scan, so it reads as a backend nothing renders. A replica count is the wrong lever regardless: the Flux controllers are deliberate singletons that hold a leader-election lease, and a second one does not serve, it waits. What a lost webhook costs is latency, not delivery, because the GitRepository still polls every minute underneath it. (chidionyema/idp#544)
      WAIVED    availability langfuse.${ESTATE_ZONE}    observability/langfuse-web: A component of the langfuse chart (langfuse-values.yaml:32,44 set replicas 1), sharing the same ClickHouse and Postgres as signoz. (chidionyema/idp#544)
      WAIVED    availability signoz.${ESTATE_ZONE}      observability/signoz-otel-collector: A component of the signoz chart; this repository renders no Deployment for it, so the values are the only lever and they follow the signoz row above. (chidionyema/idp#544)
      WAIVED    availability (behind a route)           llm/litellm-cache: One Redis holds the router's answer cache and shared cooldown counters; losing it costs cache hits, not answers -- the router keeps serving. Two plain replicas would split the cache and the cooldown state, moving the failure rather than removing it; the remedy is Sentinel or a managed Redis, not a replica count. (chidionyema/idp#1184)
timing   1020s total; slowest rungs:
         561s  ok    kyverno  platform/backstage/base platform/calico platform/chaos/mesh platform/commer
         118s  ok    idempot  catalog-gen twice over one inventory: identical (236662 bytes)
         91s  ok    incident 2026-08-24 dropped assets: 8 rows -> 8 entities, 8 db rows (two concurrent 
         65s  ok    ports    catalog-gen refuses a port claimed twice, passes the clean inventory, emits
         37s  namespace(s) DECLARE a quota, a LimitRange, a both-ways default deny and a DNS exception i
FAIL  idp-ci
rc=1
